    {"id": "PF-05", "command": "\\rm -rf /tmp/x", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Backslash prefix bypasses an alias; argv is rm."},
    {"id": "PF-06", "command": "busybox rm -rf /tmp/x", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Multi-call binary dispatch."},
    {"id": "PF-07", "command": "~/bin/fusebase deploy", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: fusebase deploy", "expected_actions": ["production_deploy"], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Tilde expansion to a user-local install."},
    {"id": "PF-08", "command": "find . -name '*.log' -exec rm {} \\;", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: rm", "expected_actions": ["destructive_file_delete"], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Bulk delete via -exec rather than -delete; `rm` appears as an ARGUMENT to find, not as a command word — a real parser must treat -exec's payload as executed."},
    {"id": "PF-09", "command": "git -C /repo push --force origin main", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: git push --force", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Global option between the program and the subcommand."},
    {"id": "PF-10", "command": "git push origin HEAD:main", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: git push main (only_when direct_to_main)", "expected_actions": ["production_deploy"], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Refspec form of a push to main."},
    {"id": "PF-11", "command": "git push origin +main", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: force push (+refspec)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "path-form", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "The leading + in a refspec IS a force push — no --force flag appears anywhere, so a flag-shaped deny pattern cannot see it and only the weaker approval rule fires."},

    {"id": "CH-01", "command": "echo ok # fusebase deploy", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Everything after # is a comment; only echo runs."},
    {"id": "CH-02", "command": "bash <<'EOF'\nfusebase deploy\nEOF", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: fusebase deploy", "expected_actions": ["production_deploy"], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "N4", "source": "constructed", "why": "bash EXECUTES its heredoc body. Ignoring heredoc bodies would make this the universal bypass."},
    {"id": "CH-03", "command": "sh <<EOF\nrm -rf /tmp/x\nEOF", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "N4", "source": "constructed", "why": "Unquoted delimiter also expands the body before sh runs it."},
    {"id": "CH-04", "command": "cat > notes.md <<'EOF'\nnever run rm -rf / on a live box\nEOF", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "N4", "source": "prerelease-report", "why": "cat is a data-only consumer; the body is written to a file, not executed."},
    {"id": "CH-05", "command": "python3 - <<'EOF'\nopen('doc.md', 'w').write('the rm -rf guard')\nEOF", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "N4", "source": "prerelease-report", "why": "The reporter hit exactly this while writing the report that describes the defect."},
    {"id": "CH-06", "command": "bash <<'EOF'\necho \"rm -rf /\"\nEOF", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "N4", "source": "constructed", "why": "Executing consumer, INERT body. Pairs with CH-02: consumer identity alone does not decide, so N4 is wrong in both directions."},
    {"id": "CH-07", "command": ": # rm -rf /tmp/x", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "No-op plus comment."},
    {"id": "CH-08", "command": "echo 'rm -rf /' > note.txt", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "comment-heredoc", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Single-quoted literal written to a file; no expansion, no execution."},

    {"id": "PC-01", "command": "git commit -m \"documents the rm -rf guard\"", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "N2", "source": "prerelease-report", "why": "Inert prose in a message payload. The shipped FP that makes an honest commit message impossible via Bash."},
    {"id": "PC-02", "command": "git commit -F docs/tmp/msg.txt", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "N3", "source": "prerelease-report", "why": "The sanctioned path today (stated in policies/command-policy.yml's header)."},
    {"id": "PC-03", "command": "git commit -m \"$(rm -rf /tmp/x)\"", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "N2", "source": "review", "why": "The substitution is expanded by the shell BEFORE git is invoked — the rm runs regardless of what git does with the message. Stripping -m opens this hole."},
    {"id": "PC-04", "command": "git commit -F \"$(scripts/gen-msg.sh && rm -rf /tmp/x)\"", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "N3", "source": "constructed", "why": "Same class as PC-03 once -F's argument is not a literal path. Red arm for 'strip the -F payload'."},
    {"id": "PC-05", "command": "grep -rn \"rm -rf\" docs/", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "A search pattern, not a command. Searching for the guard trips the guard."},
    {"id": "PC-06", "command": "rg \"git push --force\" workflows/", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Same as PC-05 against a deny pattern; this is how the ticket's own documentation is written."},
    {"id": "PC-07", "command": "sed -i 's/rm -rf//' notes.md", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Edits text; deletes nothing."},
    {"id": "PC-08", "command": "echo \"run: fusebase deploy\" >> README.md", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Documenting the deploy command is not deploying. FP direction on the require_approval stage, not just deny."},
    {"id": "PC-09", "command": "git log --grep=\"rm -rf\"", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Read-only history search."},
    {"id": "PC-10", "command": "git commit -m \"T5: add the FR-06 semantic corpus\"", "should_gate": false, "expected_rule": "(none)", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "payload-context", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Ordinary message with no gated token — the control that proves the FP is payload-dependent, not universal to -m."},

    {"id": "EN-01", "command": "echo cm0gLXJmIC90bXAveA== | base64 -d | sh", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Base64 decodes to `rm -rf /tmp/x` and is piped to a shell."},
    {"id": "EN-02", "command": "echo ZnVzZWJhc2UgZGVwbG95 | base64 -d | bash", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: fusebase deploy", "expected_actions": ["production_deploy"], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Base64 decodes to `fusebase deploy`."},
    {"id": "EN-03", "command": "printf '\\x72\\x6d -rf /tmp/x\\n' | sh", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Hex escapes produce `rm` at printf time."},
    {"id": "EN-04", "command": "$'\\x72\\x6d' -rf /tmp/x", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "ANSI-C quoting builds the command word itself; a shell parser must evaluate $'...' to see it."},
    {"id": "EN-05", "command": "echo -e \"fusebase\\x20deploy\" | sh", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-12 require: fusebase deploy", "expected_actions": ["production_deploy"], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "The separator itself is encoded, so `fusebase\\s+deploy` cannot match."},
    {"id": "EN-06", "command": "python3 -c \"import os; os.system(chr(114)+chr(109)+' -rf /tmp/x')\"", "should_gate": true, "expected_rule": "FR-06 deny: rm -rf", "expected_actions": [], "evasion_class": "encoding", "red_arm": "", "source": "constructed", "why": "Construction inside a second language — the bound on any shell-only parser."},

